therwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x\\ge 2$ and $y\\ge 2.$"] [17592186527227 "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186527228 "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0\\,\\text{or}\\,y<1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}({y}^{2}-1)}{3{y}^{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ {F}_{X}(x), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y>2 \\\\ {F}_{Y}(y), & x>1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>1,\\,y>2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${F}_{X}$ and ${F}_{Y}$ are the marginal CDFs of $X$ and $Y,$ respectively. Find the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$"] [17592186527229 "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)(y-1)}{xy}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 1.$"]}
